---
// Caution tape across the top of a planned project frame (PRD §5.3,
// increment 30): the "still building this" signal, in place of any dimming —
// the frame itself stays at full strength. Yellow-and-black diagonal bands,
// construction-site tape, in the one hazard colour (--hazard). Decorative:
// no text on it, hidden from assistive tech (the slate says "In production"
// in real text).
//
// Laid on at a slight angle and overhanging the frame, like tape stuck
// across it (the owner's pick over a flat band flush with the edges).
---

<div class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  /* Across the top sprocket strip, 8px past each side of the frame and
     turned 1.5deg. The stops are softened by a pixel so the diagonals
     render smooth rather than stair-stepped. The overhang stays inside the
     page gutters (no horizontal overflow at 320px). */
  .tape {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -0.5rem;
    top: 0.5rem;
    z-index: 1;
    height: 1.25rem;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      -45deg,
      var(--hazard) 0 11.5px,
      var(--monitor-bg) 12.5px 23.5px,
      var(--hazard) 24.5px 24.5px
    );
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px var(--shadow);
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>
